hyperactivity-is-the-theory-of-knowledge-graphs-lines-69 = cons "**Natural language prose: recursive bidirectional context-fiber quotienting.** In a text record, compression does not stop at Level-0 literal n-grams. By the record derivation of language (`docs/language-derived-from-the-record.cub` §§2–4) and equivalence-indexed repeat matching (`index-upto`, `lib/repeats.cub`), every occurrence e has a bidirectional surrounding context c₀(e). At Level 1, distinct tokens or motifs inhabiting identical bidirectional contexts acquire explicit contextual-identification paths joining them into an equivalence class [w], retaining only the intra-class index in Fib_{[·]}([w]) so zero information is lost. Re-indexing the record up to Level-1 classes (`index-upto` fed back into itself) turns previously unseen literal sequences into exact structural matches at Level 2, and iterating this fixed point builds a multi-level hierarchy of morphological, syntactic, and semantic equivalence classes deterministically from the record alone — no statistical weights and no hand-authored grammar — while keeping every occurrence path intact." (cons "" nil)
